Dear Landlord,

An update on the entrance door at 14 Lantern Mews, ahead of your answer to our approval request for an inspection.

The building manager at Brindlewick Court has told us the building file lists the flat entrance doors as fire-resisting doors. He does not have a current door-by-door inspection sheet for this door. He has also asked that no drilling or alterations are arranged without checking with building management first.

The tenant reports flaking paint on the inside face, and the door catching near the top when closing. It still latches after a firm pull.

Please bear this in mind when you reply. The painting quotation we sent (Pale Finch Decorating, £186.00) covers painting only. It does not cover the catching, and it gives no opinion on the door's fire rating. The inspection we asked you to approve is still the first step. Its cost is unknown. Any repair would be quoted separately and would need your further approval. Nothing has been assigned or scheduled.

Please let us know whether you approve the inspection.

